Design: the profile view is additive (the existing VieNeu-shaped `voices`
property stays until the QML migration in Phase 6), and every new property
reads from the capability table rather than a UI copy, so unsupported controls
can be hidden/disabled from one source of truth. Readiness is normalized into
one frozen ProfileReadiness value because the three managers disagree on shape
(ModelStatus / QwenModelStatus / QwenRuntimeStatus) and the in-process VieNeu
engine has no managed runtime at all; a raised inspect becomes state "failed"
with the error, never a stuck "checking". VieNeu's model axis MIRRORS the
official status refreshModelState already publishes instead of re-inspecting,
because that inspect re-hashes every model file — the profile refresh adds only
the device resolution for the default profile, and the whole inspection runs
off the GUI thread after first paint (the hardware probe shells out to
nvidia-smi). Switching shuts the current owner down FIRST and refuses while a
foreground job is running or the worker reports admitted work
(InferenceWorker.has_pending_work covers active, queued, and the window between
queue take and active marking), so two engines never hold the process or a
model footprint at once; the switch persists engine_profile through the same
settings file (clamped by the settings loader on read) and rebuilds the
profile-scoped clone store lazily. A failed settings write still applies the
live switch and reports the error.
